Design system (storefront)

Premium showroom palette (not Myntra retail colors):





Background #F8F8F6, cards #FFFFFF, primary sage #6E8B5E, wood accent #C49A6C, text #2D2D2D



Expressive typography (e.g. Fraunces + DM Sans via next/font)



Warm off-white + subtle wood/grain atmosphere; full-bleed hero; no card-heavy hero; Framer Motion for 2–3 intentional section/product motions



Admin UI: functional dense layout in the same palette, not a second brand exercise

Data models (MongoDB)

Collections: admins, settings, categories, brands, banners, products, enquiries.

Product (core):





Basic: name, slug, sku, categoryId, brandId, shortDescription, description, status, isFeatured, isNewArrival, viewCount



Pricing defaults: mrp, sellingPrice, discount (computed or stored)



Images (product-level fallback): ordered { url, publicId, alt, sortOrder }[]



Variants: { id, name, color?, size?, sku?, mrp, sellingPrice, stock, images[] }[] — selecting a variant swaps gallery + price/stock



Specs: dynamic { key, value }[]



Filters denormalized for listing: colors[], materials[], finishes[], inStock, minPrice, maxPrice



Timestamps: createdAt, updatedAt

Enquiry: customerName, phone, productId, productName, variantId, variantName, status (pending|contacted|completed), createdAt

Settings: store name, logo, WhatsApp number, email, address, maps embed/url, social links, opening hours

Banner: desktop/mobile image URLs, title, subtitle, button text/link, sortOrder, active

Seed script: one admin, settings, sample categories (Plywood, Laminates, Veneers, Bathroom Accessories, Door Locks, Hardware, Adhesives, Lighting, Plumbing, Power Tools), a few brands, banners, and demo products with multi-image variants.

Backend API surface

[backend/app/](backend/app/) structure: main.py, config.py, db.py, auth/, routers/, models/, schemas/, services/cloudinary.py, seed.py.

Public:





GET /api/settings, /api/banners, /api/categories, /api/brands



GET /api/products — search q, filters (category, brand, price min/max, color, material, finish, availability), sort (price_asc|price_desc|newest|popular)



GET /api/products/{slug} — increments viewCount



GET /api/products/{id}/similar



POST /api/enquiries — create enquiry (storefront quote flow)

Admin (JWT):





POST /api/admin/auth/login, GET /api/admin/auth/me



CRUD: products, categories, brands, banners



GET/PATCH /api/admin/enquiries, dashboard GET /api/admin/dashboard



GET/PUT /api/admin/settings



POST /api/admin/uploads/signature — Cloudinary signed upload params for client-side upload

Auth: bcrypt password hash, JWT access tokens, protect admin routers with dependency.

Frontend routes

Storefront ([frontend/app/(store)/](frontend/app/(store)/)):





/ — hero (Swiper banners), featured categories, best sellers, new arrivals, brands, why us, testimonials, contact/location



/categories, /categories/[slug]



/products — listing with search + sidebar filters + sort



/products/[slug] — gallery (zoom), variant picker (gallery swaps), specs, features, similar, Get Quote on WhatsApp



Contact section uses settings address/maps/WhatsApp

Admin ([frontend/app/admin/](frontend/app/admin/)):





/admin/login



/admin dashboard (totals, recent, low stock, most viewed)



Products list + create/edit (multi-image drag-reorder, variants with per-variant images/price/stock, dynamic specs)



Categories, Brands, Banners, Enquiries (status updates), Settings

Shared: API client with public base URL, auth token in httpOnly cookie or localStorage for admin (prefer httpOnly cookie via Next route handlers if straightforward; otherwise Bearer in memory + localStorage for MVP).

WhatsApp quote flow: collect name/phone → POST /api/enquiries → open https://wa.me/{number}?text=... with product/variant prefilled.

Implementation order





Scaffold monorepo, env examples, Docker Compose for MongoDB only



Backend: config, DB, auth, all models/schemas, seed, public + admin routers, Cloudinary signature



Frontend design tokens + layout shells (store + admin)



Storefront pages wired to API (home → listing → PDP)



Admin CRUD UIs ending with product editor (heaviest)



Enquiry + settings + dashboard polish



Seed demo content and README runbook

Env vars (examples)

Backend: MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET, CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET, CORS_ORIGINS, ADMIN_EMAIL, ADMIN_PASSWORD (seed)

Frontend: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET (unsigned preset only if needed; prefer signed flow)

Out of scope for Phase 1

Wishlist, cart, payments, order tracking, reviews, PDF quotes, PWA, AI search, multi-language, analytics beyond basic dashboard counts.